      "data": {
        "title": "1. Grammar: one repeatable surface relationship",
        "body": "In `utils/declarationRelationshipHandles.js`, replace the `default-view`, `summary-view`, `icon-view`, `view-sequence` and `glyph` entries of `DECLARATION_RELATIONSHIPS` with one `surface` relationship (`nodeType: 'view'`, `repeatable: true`). Keep `default-handle`, `boundary-begin`, `boundary-end`, `port` and `landing-surface` exactly as they are. Stop building the Declaration list from `PORT_SEMANTIC_RELATIONSHIPS.slice(0, 3)` (Ports keep that list unchanged; see open question 4).\n\nLegacy is preserved, NOT remapped. Declaration ports are synthesized from this list (`getNodePortDeclarations` in `utils/portDeclarations.js`), so removing the old five would orphan every legacy edge. Keep them as legacy entries (`metadata.legacy: true`): still synthesized so old edges resolve, hidden from creation UI (task 8), and never converted into `surface`. Do not touch `normalizeDeclarationRelationshipId` except for the existing `primary-view` alias. The compatibility resolver (task 3) is what reads them as one default Surface.\n\nAdd the `surface` relationship (repeatable, edge type `surface`) and stop building the Declaration list from `PORT_SEMANTIC_RELATIONSHIPS.slice(0, 3)` by naming those entries in the Declaration list itself.\n\n**Built (2026-09-24):** Added the `surface` relationship (angle 120, role `surface`, edge type `surface`, repeatable, drag-creates a View) to `DECLARATION_RELATIONSHIPS`. The five old entries stay, each marked `metadata.legacy` on its port and handle (as copies, so the Port list they share is untouched), so every old edge still lands. The list is still built from `PORT_SEMANTIC_RELATIONSHIPS.slice(0, 3)` rather than restating those three definitions, so Ports and Declarations cannot drift apart. Tests updated: `declarationDefaults.test.js`, `portDeclarations.test.js`.",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "DECLARATION_RELATIONSHIPS has one repeatable surface entry; the five old entries remain, marked legacy, so old edges keep their ports",
          "Port nodes get exactly the relationships they get today",
          "A graph whose edges use the old handle ids still resolves them (no edge is orphaned on load) and is never converted to surface edges",
          "tests/portDeclarations.test.js and tests/dynamicPortDeclarations.test.js updated and green"
        ],
