      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "2. Edge classes and the Glyph port (content repo)",
        "body": "In `mikemartinez1974/public/classes/edges/`: add a `surface` edge class (declaration → view, NO `maxOutgoing`, so many Surfaces are legal), and change `view-sequence` so `targetKinds` is `view, glyph` (a chain may end in a Glyph). Keep `maxOutgoing 1` on `view-sequence` so a chain cannot branch. Register both in the collection `classes/edges/root.node`. `shared-glyph` becomes legacy: keep it so old graphs still validate, and say so in its meaning.\n\nIn this repo: give the Glyph node an input port that accepts `view-sequence` edges (today `createDefaultGlyphNode` in `utils/systemNodeDefaults.js` only has `root`; Views get theirs from `createViewSequencePorts`). Check `utils/edgeLegality.js` and `tests/coreEdgeClasses.test.js`.\n\nOrdering matters: the app fetches these classes from github, so the content-repo change must be published before or with the app change, and the app must behave sensibly when it reads the OLD classes (see task 9).\n\n**Built (2026-09-24):** Added `classes/edges/surface/root.node` (declaration → view, no limit) and changed `view-sequence` to end at `view, glyph` (still one out, one in, so a chain cannot branch). The collection lists `surface` first. Generated with the same generator as the other core classes; the six untouched classes were verified identical (timestamps aside) and were not rewritten. A Glyph now gets a `sequence-in` port (`utils/portDeclarations.js`). `tests/coreEdgeClasses.test.js` and `tests/edgeLegality.test.js` updated, with new cases for a second Surface, a glyph-first Surface being refused, and a chain ending in a glyph.\n\nNOT DONE: publishing. The content repo change is local. Until it is published the app finds no `surface` class and refuses nothing (`edgeClassCatalog`), which is safe.",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A Declaration can draw two `surface` edges without EDGE_CLASS_ILLEGAL_CONNECTION",
          "A view-sequence edge from a View to a Glyph is legal; a second outgoing view-sequence edge from the same View is not",
          "Old graphs using shared-glyph still validate",
          "tests/coreEdgeClasses.test.js and tests/edgeLegality.test.js updated and green"
        ],
