      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "3. One chain resolver, per Surface",
        "body": "Add a pure module (extend `utils/viewSequence.js` or a sibling) exposing `collectSurfaceChains(graph)`: for each `surface` edge from the Declaration, walk `view-sequence` edges from its head and return `{ surfaceId, head, views[], glyph }`. Reuse the existing loop guard (stops at a node already seen). The glyph is the chain's terminal node; malformed chains follow the rule chosen in open question 2.\n\nDeterminism is the resolver's job, not the edge classes': an imported file bypasses the editor's rules, so a chain that branches (follow the first outgoing edge in graph order, diagnose), cycles (stop at the first repeated node), has a glyph mid-chain (the glyph ends the walk) or has a `surface` edge whose head is not a View (skip it, diagnose) must all resolve without exception and identically every time.\n\nLegacy synthesis is the compatibility layer: a graph with NO `surface` edges but with role-wired default/summary/icon views (and `shared-glyph` or `declaration.data.glyph`) yields exactly ONE default Surface built from them, never one Surface per relationship. `collectViewSequence` already does the view part of this through `ROLE_SEQUENCE`; extend it, do not duplicate it. Keep `collectViewSequence` and `resolveViewByName` working for their current callers (`addressedView.js`, `graphNodeContract.js`) by implementing them on top of the new function.\n\nDepends on: tasks 1, 2.\n\n**Built (2026-09-24):** New pure module `utils/surfaceChains.js`: `collectSurfaceChains`, `resolveSurface`, `surfaceViewNodes`, `resolveSurfaceViewByName`. The Surface id is `edge.data.surfaceId` (else the edge id). Legacy synthesis yields exactly one default Surface from `collectViewSequence` plus the shared glyph. Every malformed case resolves deterministically and never throws: a cycle stops at the first repeated node, a branch follows the first outgoing edge, a glyph ends the walk, a chain reaching a non-View stops, a head that is not a View is skipped, a duplicate id keeps the first, and a missing default falls to the first Surface. Each is diagnosed with a `SURFACE_*` code. `graphNodeContract.js` and `addressedView.js` now call `resolveSurfaceViewByName`; `collectViewSequence` is unchanged. `tests/surfaceChains.test.js` (15 tests).",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A graph with two `surface` edges returns two chains, each with its own views and glyph",
          "A legacy default/summary/icon graph returns exactly one chain equivalent to what collectViewSequence returns today, plus its glyph",
          "Cycles, a glyph mid-chain, views after the glyph and a chain with no glyph all resolve deterministically per the rule in open question 2, with no exception",
          "tests/viewSequence.test.js keeps passing; new cases cover the above"
        ],
