      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "6. Validator and defaults",
        "body": "`validators/validateGraphInvariants.js` `requiredRootRoles`: stop requiring default-view, summary-view, icon-view and glyph as separate relationships. Require at least one Surface (a legacy role-wired one counts) and keep `landing-surface`. Add warnings, not errors, for a chain problem: `SURFACE_CHAIN_NO_GLYPH` (chain does not end in a Glyph), `SURFACE_CHAIN_GLYPH_NOT_LAST` (nodes after a Glyph), `SURFACE_CHAIN_BRANCH`, `SURFACE_CHAIN_CYCLE`, `SURFACE_HEAD_NOT_VIEW`, `SURFACE_DUPLICATE_ID` and `SURFACE_DEFAULT_MISSING` (defaultSurfaceId names no Surface). Keep `LANDING_SURFACE_MULTIPLE`.\n\n`createDefaultGraph` and `createDefaultDeclarationNode` in `utils/systemNodeDefaults.js` should author the new shape: a `surface` edge to a detail View that chains through summary and icon Views to a Glyph, plus the landing surface. Check `GraphCrud.js` (about line 1451 lists the view roles) and the MCP tools in `scripts/mcp/` for anything that authors the old edges.\n\nDepends on: tasks 1, 3.\n\n**Built (2026-09-24):** Validator: `validateGraphInvariants.js` reads `collectSurfaceChains`. A graph that draws Surfaces is not asked for default-view, summary-view, icon-view and glyph, but still owes `landing-surface`; a legacy graph is held to exactly what it was. Chain problems are warnings: `SURFACE_CHAIN_NO_GLYPH`, `_GLYPH_NOT_LAST`, `_BRANCH`, `_CYCLE`, `_NOT_VIEW`, `SURFACE_HEAD_NOT_VIEW`, `SURFACE_DUPLICATE_ID`, `SURFACE_DEFAULT_MISSING`.\n\nDefaults: `createDefaultGraph` now authors one Surface: a `surface` edge (id `default`) to the Detail View, `view-sequence` links Detail → Summary → Icon → a Glyph, and the landing surface. A new graph validates with zero warnings, resolves detail, summary, icon and then its glyph as the room shrinks, and derives the same node class as the same graph written with the older relationships. Two consumers keyed off the old `default-view` edge and would have lost a new graph, and now fall back to the first View of the default Surface: `graphNavigationAddress.js` (a graph would have read as \"graph-only\", losing landing focus) and the library member listing in `graphNodeContract.js` (a collection would not have exposed its root port). `GraphCrud.js`, `scripts/`, `lib/`, `app/` and `.skills/` were checked: nothing else authors the old shape.\n\nAlso fixed: `GraphCrud.js` `validateHandlePair` rejected edges to a View's `sequence-in` and `sequence-out` (\"handle not found\") because it only read explicitly authored handles; it now accepts any port the node's semantic declarations provide. Browser smoke `tests/browser/workspaceNodeSelection.smoke.cjs` passes against new-shape graphs.",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A default new graph validates with zero warnings and its Declaration has one Surface ending in a Glyph",
          "A legacy graph gets no NEW warnings from this change (compare warnings on a sample of public/ graphs before and after)",
          "A Declaration with a chain that has no Glyph produces exactly one SURFACE_CHAIN_NO_GLYPH warning",
          "tests/declarationDefaults.test.js and tests/declarationPrimaryViewValidation.test.js updated and green"
        ],
