      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "8. Authoring UI for Surfaces and chains",
        "body": "Move the authoring surface from three named handles to one `surface` handle plus chain editing.\n- `GraphEditor.js` handle-drag creation (`startHandleKey === 'default-view' | 'summary-view' | 'icon-view'` and the `semanticViewData` payload/level mapping): dragging from the `surface` handle creates the first View of a new Surface; dragging from a View's `sequence-out` handle creates the next View, or a Glyph, and connects it.\n- Declaration view-binding editors in `PropertiesPanel.js` (about lines 655 and 975) and `DynamicViewNode.js` (about lines 180 and 201, the `declaration-view-binding` field type): show the Surfaces and their chains instead of three named slots; let the author reorder a chain and see where its Glyph is.\n- Label and role lists that name the old handles: `FixedNode.js`, `PortNode.js`, `utils/nodeVisibilityRoles.js`, `utils/viewExposure.js`, and the Declaration rows in `ManifestNode.js` (`Default Port`, `Exposed Entries`).\n\nKeep GraphEditorContent.js out of it; put chain-editing helpers in a pure module with tests.\n\nDepends on: tasks 1, 2, 3.\n\n**Built (2026-09-24):** Built and checked in the live editor: the `surface` handle drags out a Detail View and a `surface` edge that carries the next free Surface id (`default`, `surface-2`, …); a View's next-view handle (`sequence-out`) drags out the next View and its `view-sequence` edge; unused legacy Declaration handles are hidden (a legacy handle shows only while an edge uses it; `isUnusedLegacyHandle` in `handleVisibility.js`, applied in `HandleLayer.js`); the Declaration editor's Surfaces tab lists every Surface with its Views and Glyph and any problem, and the Default Surface select offers the real Surface ids (`SurfaceChainList.js`). Tests: `surfaceChains.test.js`, `graphCrud.test.js`.\n\nNOT DONE: reordering a chain from the UI; creating a Glyph by drag (a Glyph is added from the toolbar and connected to the last View's next-view handle); the `PropertiesPanel.js` binding editors and the `FixedNode.js` / `PortNode.js` / `viewExposure.js` label lists still name the old handles; a legacy graph that draws its first `surface` edge stops being read as legacy, so its old default, summary and icon views drop out of its presentation until they are chained.",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A new Surface can be created, extended View by View, and ended with a Glyph using only handle drags",
          "The Properties panel shows every Surface on a Declaration with its chain and terminal Glyph",
          "Reordering views in a chain updates the edges, and a chain that would put a Glyph mid-chain is prevented or warned per open question 2",
          "No UI string still refers to the retired relationships as if they were current"
        ],
