      "data": {
        "title": "9. Legacy graphs: read-compat, optional migration",
        "body": "Old graphs must keep working with no rewrite. Verify the synthesis in task 3 against real graphs: pick a spread from `public/` (roughly 131 use summary-view, 146 use icon-view, 7 use default-view), load each, and check they resolve the same views and the same glyph as before. Add a test that a legacy graph and its hand-migrated `surface`-chain equivalent resolve identically at several occupancies.\n\nPer AGENTS.md's rewrite rule there is no bulk normalization. If open question 3 chooses to offer migration, add an opt-in script modeled on `npm run migrate:events` (`utils/eventMigration.js`): dry-run by default, `--write` to apply, preserves graphId, nodeId and addresses, and refuses a graph it cannot migrate losslessly.\n\nDepends on: tasks 3, 4, 5; open question 3.\n\n**Built (2026-09-24):** Read-compat verified against the real library: over all 546 Declaration graphs in `twilite/public` none uses `surface` edges, none threw, the legacy Surface's views match `collectViewSequence` in every case, and glyph resolution matches the old logic exactly. The level lookup and ladder were compared over the 178 graphs with an exact `declaration` node: zero differences. Only one graph has Views wired through the old roles, so most graphs get their presentation from the graph-wide scan, which is unchanged. Tests cover a legacy graph resolving identically with and without a Surface requested, and a Surface-written graph deriving the same node class as its legacy equivalent.\n\nNOT DONE: the opt-in migration script (question 3 made it optional), and a visual check that sampled graphs render the same.",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A sampled set of at least 20 varied public/ graphs render the same View and Glyph at each level before and after the change",
          "A legacy graph and its migrated equivalent resolve identically (automated test)",
          "If a migration script ships: dry-run by default, idempotent, lossless, with a test"
        ],
