      "data": {
        "title": "10. Smoke test: two Surfaces, bad chains",
        "body": "The smoke test the Declaration graph asks for. Build a fixture graph (in `tests/`, not the public library) with two Surfaces, each chain ending in its own Glyph, and assert the unit-level behavior of tasks 3 to 6. Then a live check in the running app (the repo has a pattern in `tests/browser/*.smoke.cjs`): open it in the workspace and step through every zoom level, confirming each Surface's ladder resolves independently and each shows its own Glyph at the smallest.\n\nThen deliberately do it wrong, and record what actually happens for each: Glyph mid-chain, Views after the Glyph, no Glyph, a cycle, two Surfaces sharing a View, a `surface` edge to a non-View. The results settle open question 2 and go back into the Declaration graph's Ports node, where the malformed-chain rule is currently marked as a guess.\n\nDepends on: tasks 3 to 6 (unit level), plus task 8 for authoring the fixtures by hand.\n\n**Built (2026-09-24):** Unit level done in `tests/surfaceChains.test.js`: a two-Surface, two-Glyph fixture, and every malformed case has a recorded deterministic outcome with a test. Live: a two-Surface graph (a canvas Surface and a 3D-only Surface) loaded in the running editor and was stepped from zoom 0.52 to the 0.1 floor in 14 steps; the card resized smoothly, and there were no page errors. The malformed-chain rule is written into the Declaration primitive graph.\n\nNOT DONE: the live check does not prove WHICH glyph the card drew (the unit tests do); and the malformed case \"two Surfaces sharing one View\" is not recorded.",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A fixture with two Surfaces and two Glyphs passes unit tests and a live zoom walk",
          "Every malformed case above has a recorded, deterministic outcome and a test",
          "primitives/declaration Ports node updated: the \"guess\" wording replaced by the verified rule"
        ],
