      "data": {
        "title": "11. Web view and 3D view as Surfaces",
        "body": "The reason for all of this: the web view and the planned 3D view are Surfaces, and they should share this one mechanism instead of each having its own. This task is BLOCKED on open question 6 and has not been investigated: nobody has yet read `Nodes/ThreeDNode.js` or how the web view (`components/PersistentIframe.js`, the `embed` node type, `Nodes/DynamicViewNode.js` web payloads) picks its content.\n\nStart by writing down how each of those two picks what to show today, then express each as a Surface on the Declaration model: a chain of Views (payload kind `web` / `3d`) ending in a Glyph, asked for by a host that names it. The `context` field proposed by the Surface primitive graph (`declaration.surfaces[].context`) is the likely place a host says which Surface it wants.\n\nDepends on: tasks 3, 5, 7. Question 6 is decided: an explicit Surface request wins, context picks a default, capability filters.\n\n**Built (2026-09-24):** How each works today (read from the code): the 3D \"view\" is only a standalone node type `3d` (`Nodes/ThreeDNode.js`, label \"3D View\"): a Three.js scene with a fixed demo cube and OrbitControls that reads nothing from its data except `_semanticLevel`. No View has a `node.3d.*` payload and nothing renders one. The web view is not a component but a host tag already in payload names: `node.web.detail`, `node.web.summary`, `node.web.icon`, `editor.web`, `icon.web`, `document.web`, `graph.web` (149 references), aliased to detail, summary and icon by `viewSequence.js`, and rendered by `DynamicViewNode.js` (with `PersistentIframe.js` for html and embeds). So the host already lives per View in the payload; what was missing was a Surface-level choice.\n\nBuilt: `viewHost(view)` reads the host from a payload (`web`, `3d`, `vr`, `ar`, `map`, `native`; a View naming none is written for any host), `surfaceRenderableBy`, and `resolveSurface(graph, surfaceId, { hosts })`: an explicit request wins, the default answers otherwise, and a Surface the host cannot render is never chosen. The ladder, glyph and level lookup all follow it. Tested with a web canvas Surface and a 3D Surface.\n\nNOT DONE: there is no 3D View renderer, so no host yet asks for the 3D Surface; a host declaring its own context to pick the default is not built.",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A short note in this graph records how the web view and 3D view resolve today",
          "The web view and 3D view are each reachable as a Surface through the same resolver, with no second resolution path left behind",
          "A graph with a graph-canvas Surface and a 3D Surface shows the right one for the right host"
        ],
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
