      "data": {
        "title": "12. Docs, LLM prompt, and the Surface primitive",
        "body": "Do this LAST, after the behavior ships, because AGENTS.md says the authoritative contracts win over code and examples, and `OnboardLLM.md` is what external chatbots are taught to write.\n- Authoritative docs: `public/library/documentation/contracts/nodes/graph-native-node-composition.md`, `public/library/documentation/contracts/model/twilite-structural-model-inventory.md`, `docs/twilite-native-graph-v1.md`.\n- AGENTS.md primitive table row for `declaration` (\"Declaration relationships\": default-view, landing-surface, summary-view, icon-view, glyph, port).\n- `public/library/documentation/OnboardLLM.md` and the DIVERGENT copy in the twilite-zone repo (AGENTS.md flags this): decide whether to reconcile them.\n- The Surface primitive graph (`primitives/surface/root.node`): its Contract and Ports nodes still say the four old relationships remain and that Views tag themselves with `data.surfaceId`. Reconcile with open question 1.\n- Update the Declaration primitive graph's \"Status: target model, not yet in code\" wording to match what shipped, and record the Ports decision (open question 4).\n\n**Built (2026-09-24):** Updated to describe Surfaces, and validated: `graph-native-node-composition.md` (Declaration contract table, the definition of a Surface, legacy relationships, relationship authority, agent checklist), `docs/twilite-native-graph-v1.md` (Root Composition), `twilite-structural-model-inventory.md`, `AGENTS.md` (Declaration relationships), and `OnboardLLM.md` (tables, do and don't lists, a rewritten worked example, growing a graph, the checklist). The OnboardLLM starter was parsed and validated: no errors or warnings, and it resolves to one Surface, `Plan`, ending in the glyph `Checklist`. The Surface primitive graph was reconciled with what shipped (Surface identity is the edge, no View `surfaceId`, host rules, what is and is not built), and the Declaration primitive graph's status text now matches. Both validate clean.\n\nNOT DONE: the divergent OnboardLLM copy in `twilite-zone` was not touched; it defers to the composition contract for the Declaration model and names none of the old relationships except in passing, so it needs a reconcile only if you want the two copies to converge.",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "No authoritative doc, AGENTS.md, OnboardLLM.md or primitive graph describes the retired relationships as current",
          "The Declaration primitive graph no longer says \"target model\"",
          "The Surface primitive graph and the Declaration primitive graph agree on how a View belongs to a Surface"
        ],
