      "data": {
        "title": "2. What does a host do with a badly ordered chain?",
        "body": "Nothing yet defines this. Cases: a Glyph in the middle, Views after the Glyph, no Glyph, a cycle, a chain that branches, a `surface` edge that points at a non-View.\n\nRecommendation, to be checked by the smoke test (task 10): the walk stops at the first Glyph and ignores anything after it (validator warns); a chain with no Glyph falls back to `declaration.data.glyph` and then to the generic mark (warns); a cycle stops at the first repeated node (already how `collectViewSequence` behaves); branching is prevented by `maxOutgoing 1` on `view-sequence`; a `surface` edge to a non-View is illegal by edge class. All of these degrade to something visible rather than to nothing.",
        "status": "resolved",
        "resolutionPath": "Decided: visible fallback plus diagnostics, and a deterministic resolver for branches, cycles and a glyph mid-chain (imported files bypass edge-class rules). The smoke test (task 10) records the verified outcomes.",
        "owner": "",
        "prominence": "high",
        "_classBinding": {
