      "data": {
        "title": "3. Legacy graphs: read-compat only, or also a migration script?",
        "body": "About 131 graphs in `public/` use `summary-view` and 146 use `icon-view`, and the content repo holds more. Task 3's synthesis makes them all keep working with no change, which is the safe minimum.\n\nRecommendation: read-compat only for now, with an opt-in dry-run-by-default script available but not run over the library, because AGENTS.md forbids bulk-normalizing by shape and a lossless conversion has to preserve node ids and view resolution values. Say if you want the library migrated, and in which order (the primitives and classes first, say).",
        "status": "resolved",
        "resolutionPath": "Decided: read-compat only. Old relationships are preserved when reading and exactly one default Surface is synthesized from them. No bulk migration of the library; an opt-in dry-run script is optional.",
        "owner": "",
