      "data": {
        "title": "4. Do Port nodes move to Surfaces too?",
        "body": "Port nodes share the Declaration's default-view / summary-view / icon-view / glyph relationships (`PORT_SEMANTIC_RELATIONSHIPS`) and have their own per-level presentation (`resolveGraphPortPresentation` in `graphNodeContract.js`). The Declaration graph only speaks about the Declaration.\n\nRecommendation: leave Ports exactly as they are in this pass. Ports resolve per level for a specific exposed entry point, which is a different question from how the graph as a whole presents. Task 1 only needs to stop the Declaration reading the shared list. Revisit once Surfaces are working, since two vocabularies for the same idea will eventually feel wrong.",
        "status": "resolved",
        "resolutionPath": "Decided: Port nodes are unchanged in this pass.",
        "owner": "",
        "prominence": "high",
