      "data": {
        "title": "5. Where does the Declaration's default identity-card View live?",
        "body": "To resolve \"like any class node\", the Declaration needs a View definition. Options: (a) built into the app, shipped as code and used through the same resolver; (b) a class graph in the content library, fetched like the edge classes.\n\nRecommendation: (a). A Declaration is needed to read any graph at all, including the collection that would supply (b), and the app already lives with \"until it has been read there are no default classes\" for edge classes. A library override can be layered on later without changing the resolver. Decide before task 7.",
        "status": "resolved",
        "resolutionPath": "Decided: until the Declaration template exists (question 8), the default identity-card View ships in the app and resolves through the same resolver. Once the template exists the card comes from it.",
        "owner": "",
        "prominence": "high",
