      "data": {
        "title": "6. How does a host say which Surface it wants, and do web and 3D map one-to-one?",
        "body": "You said the web view and the 3D view are both Surfaces. What is not yet written down is how a host asks: by Surface id, by a `context` value (the field the Surface primitive graph proposes as `declaration.surfaces[].context`), or by the View payload kind (`web`, `3d`). And whether each is exactly one Surface, or a Surface can hold Views of more than one kind.\n\nRecommendation: a host asks by `context` and falls back to the default Surface; a Surface's Views can carry any payload kind, so \"3D\" is a Surface whose Views happen to be 3D. Needs your call before task 5 is finished and before task 11 starts. I have not read the web view or 3D code yet (see task 11).",
        "status": "resolved",
        "resolutionPath": "Decided: an explicit Surface request wins; host context only picks a default; capability (HTML, 3D) filters out Surfaces the host cannot render. Web and 3D are each a Surface; their Views carry the payload kind.",
        "owner": "",
        "prominence": "high",
