      "data": {
        "title": "7. Can a graph expose only a Glyph, with no View?",
        "body": "A chain is View → … → Glyph, and a `surface` edge points at the first View. That rule leaves no way to say \"this graph is only a glyph\".",
        "status": "resolved",
        "resolutionPath": "Decided by the owner: no. Every Surface begins with a View. A graph that wants to show as just a glyph authors an icon View that renders a glyph and ends its chain with its ordinary Glyph.",
        "owner": "",
        "prominence": "high",
