    {
      "id": "dsc-question-8",
      "type": "open-question",
      "label": "Open Question",
      "position": {
        "x": -1200,
        "y": 2800
      },
      "width": 340,
      "height": 340,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "8. How does an author give the Declaration node its own Views?",
        "body": "Decided so far: the Declaration node's own card is a separate presentation from the graph's Surfaces, has a built-in default View, and resolves through the same resolver as class and template nodes. Not decided: how an author overrides it with Views of their own. A relationship on the Declaration (for example a `node-view` port), a field naming a View, or a class-style binding are all possible, and each has different consequences for the Declaration primitive graph. Not needed for task 7; only for letting authors customize the card.",
        "status": "resolved",
        "resolutionPath": "Decided by the owner: no new relationship. A Port, and the Declaration as the implicit root Port, connects to Views through the relationships it already has. The Declaration node's own presentation comes from a Declaration template graph, which holds all of its parts, and resolves through that graph by the ordinary class binding, exactly as any class or template node does. An author who wants a different card uses a different template. (A reserved Surface id was proposed and withdrawn.)",
        "owner": "",
        "prominence": "high",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "open-question",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/open-question.node-class.node",
